{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006916-mcguffin-for-a-mage-game","id":1006916,"title":"Mcguffin for a Mage Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T17:27:18-08:00","id":1006916,"title":"Mcguffin for a Mage Game","content":"Need an Umbral Mcguffin for a Mage game within the next 33 hours.<br /> <br /> Here's the scenario. My mages managed to get a favour out of some Talons of Horus, and now they need to repay the favour.<br /> A Surtur has a &quot;thing&quot; that they want/need. Problem is that Surtur by their very nature are confrontational spirits who do not deal in diplomacy. As the Talons of Horus are forbidden from engaging in combat with anyone who fights for Gaia, this means they need an intermediary to help out with this.<br /> <br /> This means our Mages will have to either trick, steal, or challenge their way to part the Surtur from the &quot;thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> So here's my problem, I'm drawing a blank on what this &quot;thing&quot; would be. Most of the items in WTA detail things that Werewolves would use rather than what other spirits might use.<br /> <br /> In 33 hours it's game time, so if you can suggest anything appropriate, please help before then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:35:49-08:00","id":1007004,"title":"","content":"A fiery sword is sort of the default item one associates with Surtur. Though his personal one might be a bit much.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a mystic fire started with his sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T21:27:47-08:00","id":1007023,"title":"","content":"The Surtur is guarding an egg, a powerful spirit that is waiting to be born/re-born. The time for the Surtur to pass the egg on so the Talons of Horus can deliver it is now. The Surtur however thinks it is too dangerous and does not want to pass the egg on. The Talons need the players to retrieve the egg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T15:05:23-08:00","id":1007449,"title":"","content":"It's a bit of a bland answer, but how about a Pathstone for a caern? Or perhaps something rare from one of the planetary realms? Seeds of Eshtarra, for example, are very potent and useful. A number of the realms in Rage Across the Heavens have unique talens that could be claimed.<br /> <br /> Or... if you REALLY want to complicate their lives, I recall a Maeljin Incarna or two happen to have weaknesses linked to lost items that could be hidden in the Umbra somewhere. (Book of the Wyrm 20th)<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you could take something from first edition and decide it has a voidstone. It's a little pebble that can erase a victim from existence. Innocuous enough, but handing one over to someone would carry some heavy baggage as well, depending on where you think they plan to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 11-23-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}